cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "More than a Hack 2027: Frame-level Ball Possession"
message: "If you use this benchmark, its data or its metrics, please cite it."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A frame-level ball-possession benchmark built on one full professional football match
  (FC Barcelona vs Athletic Club, LaLiga EA Sports 2024-25, matchday 2). Participants label
  each of 199,319 video frames as home in possession, away in possession, or dead ball.
  Entries are ranked by spellF1, a possession-interval metric that scores each possession
  once rather than each frame, and macroF1 is reported alongside it. The repository provides
  the scorer, a public 5-minute ground truth and reference baselines; the full-match ground
  truth is held private.
authors:
  - name: "Metrica Sports"
  - name: "Barça Innovation Hub"
repository-code: "https://github.com/metrica-sports/more-than-a-hack-2027"
license: MIT
